gpui_macos: don't query the tab group of a window that doesn't use tabbing

`Window::new` calls `PlatformWindow::tab_bar_visible`, which sends
`-[NSWindow tabGroup]`. On first use AppKit creates the window's tab group and
`NSWindowStackController`. For a window opened without a tabbing identifier,
GPUI has already disabled automatic window tabbing, so the window cannot show
a native tab bar. Return false for it without touching the tab group.

Measured on a cold first window (hosted macos-15, debug, Time Profiler): the
`tabGroup` call took ~590 ms wall, 506 ms of it blocked off-CPU.

